    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_10",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Renée Montagne (pronounced Mon-TAIN) is an American radio journalist and was the co-host (with Steve Inskeep and David Greene) of National Public Radio's weekday morning news program, \"Morning Edition\", from May 2004 to November 11, 2016. Montagne and Inskeep succeeded longtime host Bob Edwards, initially as interim replacements, and Greene joined the team in 2012. Montagne had served as a correspondent and occasional host since 1989. She usually broadcasts from NPR West in Culver City, California, a Los Angeles suburb.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.9999999954842776,
      "temperature": 0.9999999954842776,
      "expanded": false,
      "visit_count": 0,
